@prefix orexis: <http://example.org/orexis#> .
@prefix onboarding: <http://example.org/orexis/onboarding#> .
@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .

<> a orexis:OntologyGraph .    # this document is one graph, and this is what it is

#  OREXIS ONBOARDING.
#  THE KINDS OF DOCUMENT ONBOARDING READS AND NO AGENT DOES (a-documents-kind-says-who-reads-it).
#  A kind says who reads a document, and every reader loads only the kinds it reads: the agent's
#  boot passes over a graph whose kind its T-Box does not declare. These are declared here, beside
#  the code that reads them and outside `agent/`, which the image does not copy — so no agent's
#  vocabulary can say what they are, and its ignorance of them is structural rather than a list of
#  file names kept out of its filesystem.

onboarding:HardwareGraph a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf orexis:Graph ; rdfs:label "Hardware graph" ;
    rdfs:comment "The boards, pins, parts and wire colours a world is built from, read by `orexis-firmware` alone to write a board's config.h. The GRAPH has a kind and the parts inside it stay untyped, since a vocabulary one string-filling reader uses checks nothing (knowledge/domain/onboarding/onboarding.md)." .

onboarding:DeploymentGraph a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf orexis:Graph ; rdfs:label "Deployment graph" ;
    rdfs:comment "What must be running for a world to be a society and where each thing answers - a broker's address, a series store, a container's image - read by onboarding alone and handed to an agent as environment. Never a credential (knowledge/domain/onboarding/deployment.md)." .

onboarding:RequirementGraph a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf orexis:Graph ; rdfs:label "Requirement graph" ;
    rdfs:comment "What a world must state of a package's or a domain's words: SHACL shapes the package or domain owning the words ships in a document of this kind beside its ontology, and `orexis-onboard` holds a world to before anything is granted. Read by onboarding alone, since what an agent holds is accepted and revised once it runs and a sovereign's document may be garbage only before it is believed; no agent loads one (knowledge/domain/onboarding/requirement.md, #838)." .

onboarding:ViewGraph a owl:Class ; rdfs:subClassOf orexis:Graph ; rdfs:label "View graph" ;
    rdfs:comment "How a domain's history is drawn in a replay: the views a domain ships beside its ontology, each of a kind `orexis-replay` renders, saying in the domain's own words which of the history's points place what on it. Read by `orexis-replay` alone, which draws what the history holds and never a belief; no agent loads one (knowledge/domain/onboarding/view.md)." .

onboarding:Grid a owl:Class ; rdfs:label "Grid" ;
    rdfs:comment "A view of a plane of whole numbers, two axes, a cell per position: each agent's things as fixed and as seen, the steps its plan drives to, what it asked with and what it laid of its peers - said and foreseen - and its conflicts, at every instant of a replay (knowledge/domain/onboarding/view.md)." .

onboarding:across a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:label "across" ;
    rdfs:domain onboarding:Grid ; rdfs:range onboarding:Axis ;
    rdfs:comment "A grid's axis drawn from left to right." .

onboarding:down a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:label "down" ;
    rdfs:domain onboarding:Grid ; rdfs:range onboarding:Axis ;
    rdfs:comment "A grid's axis drawn from top to bottom." .

onboarding:Axis a owl:Class ; rdfs:label "Axis" ;
    rdfs:comment "One axis of a view, said as what places a thing on it in each kind of point the history holds: `holds`, `fixes`, `offsets` and `moves`, each stated where the domain has one (knowledge/domain/onboarding/view.md)." .

onboarding:holds a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:label "holds" ;
    rdfs:domain onboarding:Axis ; rdfs:range rdf:Property ;
    rdfs:comment "The predicate of a constraint's key a holding's value on the axis is said under, as coordination writes a holding's point." .

onboarding:fixes a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:label "fixes" ;
    rdfs:domain onboarding:Axis ; rdfs:range rdf:Property ;
    rdfs:comment "The property an observation of a thing's own position on the axis observes: its feature is where the reading puts it." .

onboarding:offsets a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:label "offsets" ;
    rdfs:domain onboarding:Axis ; rdfs:range rdf:Property ;
    rdfs:comment "The property an observation of an offset on the axis observes: its feature, a sample, is where the reading puts it from the thing hosting the sample as that thing was fixed, and is drawn as the thing it is a sample of, where it is one; a reading outside the range its sensor declares sees nothing." .

onboarding:moves a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:label "moves" ;
    rdfs:domain onboarding:Axis ; rdfs:range rdf:Property ;
    rdfs:comment "The parameter an action takes that says where a step puts a thing on the axis, as a step's point is tagged with it." .

onboarding:monitored a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:label "monitored" ;
    rdfs:domain onboarding:DeploymentGraph ;
    rdfs:comment "Said by a world's own deployment graph of itself, `<> onboarding:monitored true`: the world's agents write their metrics, so each is minted a metrics bucket and told of it, and the world gets a health dashboard. Absent is no - metrics are the admins' instrumentation and a world opts in - and a world saying it where the installation serves metrics from no store is refused at onboarding (knowledge/domain/onboarding/deployment.md)." .

#  THE INSTALLATION'S WORDS (knowledge/domain/onboarding/deployment.md). The installation is the
#  deployment graph of what every world shares, `infra/installation.ttl`; these are what it says
#  of each shared service. An address is `schema:url`, as a broker's already was.

onboarding:SeriesStore a owl:Class ; rdfs:label "Series store" ;
    rdfs:comment "Where every agent's series is written, a bucket of its own in the store's organisation - InfluxDB 2 today. `orexis-influx` mints buckets and tokens in it and `orexis-compose` tells each agent where it is (knowledge/domain/kernel/series.md)." .

onboarding:serves a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:label "serves" ;
    rdfs:domain onboarding:SeriesStore ; rdfs:range onboarding:SeriesPurpose ;
    rdfs:comment "A purpose a series store is told to an agent for: history is served by exactly one store, metrics by one or none, and `orexis-compose` tells an agent the store's url and organisation under the purpose's keys, `INFLUX_<PURPOSE>_URL` and `_ORG` - metrics' only where the agent's world is `onboarding:monitored`. Two purposes may name one store, by coincidence and not by design (knowledge/domain/kernel/series.md)." .

onboarding:SeriesPurpose a owl:Class ; rdfs:label "Series purpose" ;
    rdfs:comment "What a series is written for, which decides the bucket it goes to, the credential that opens it and how long it keeps a point. Two, and the agent's code names each (`agent.series`): history and metrics." .

onboarding:History a onboarding:SeriesPurpose ; rdfs:label "history" ;
    rdfs:comment "What happened: every observation, every step taken and how it ended, every plan published, and what coordination asked with, laid and concluded, contributed by the package that decides each. The record, kept for good, in the bucket the one series had before purposes." .

onboarding:Metrics a onboarding:SeriesPurpose ; rdfs:label "metrics" ;
    rdfs:comment "How the agent is doing, for whoever administers it: each loaded package's gauges and tallied events and the runtime's own, written once a window of `onboarding:intervalSeconds`. Written only by the agents of a world that is `onboarding:monitored`, to a bucket of their own opened for writing alone, and kept as long as `onboarding:retentionDays` says." .

onboarding:intervalSeconds a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:label "interval seconds" ;
    rdfs:domain onboarding:SeriesPurpose ;
    rdfs:comment "How many seconds of real time one window of a purpose's points covers, stated by the installation of metrics: an agent tallies its events in memory and writes the window, with every gauge sampled once, at its end. `orexis-compose` tells it to each agent of a monitored world as `METRICS_INTERVAL_S`; absent, the agent keeps sixty (agent/metrics.py)." .

onboarding:retentionDays a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:label "retention days" ;
    rdfs:domain onboarding:SeriesPurpose ;
    rdfs:comment "How many days a purpose's buckets keep a point, stated by the installation; absent is for ever. `orexis-influx` sets it on a bucket it makes and puts it right on one it finds kept otherwise." .

onboarding:SeriesView a owl:Class ; rdfs:label "Series view" ;
    rdfs:comment "Where the series is drawn for a person - the operator's view of every world at once, Grafana today. `orexis-infra-compose` runs it on the port its url states." .

onboarding:organisation a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:label "organisation" ;
    rdfs:domain onboarding:SeriesStore ;
    rdfs:comment "The organisation on a series store that every bucket is minted in and every agent is told of. Where, not what may be done there: the token is a credential and is in no graph." .

onboarding:image a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:label "image" ;
    rdfs:comment "The container image a shared service runs, pinned where a newer one would change what the service guarantees - read by `orexis-infra-compose`." .

onboarding:allocatesFrom a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:label "allocates from" ;
    rdfs:comment "Where the installation allocates a broker the urls no world asserts for it: one url per scheme, each at the first port of its run, and a broker is given the lowest slot n at which every one of them, its port raised by n, is free on its host. What is allocated is a derived deployment graph, `infra/installation.derived.ttl`, and an allocation made is kept, so adding a world moves no other's port. An asserted url always wins (knowledge/decisions/a-documents-kind-says-who-reads-it.md, its amendment)." .
